      "observed": "EPD connector J4 pin 13 (SCL) and SKW92A U11 pin 45 (HW_RESET) share NET0024. The EPD clock is therefore connected directly to the module's hardware-reset input.",
      "expected": "The EPD clock should connect to a suitable serial/GPIO signal, not the module's HW_RESET input. The specification maps the EPD serial clock to a separate module signal.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "J4 pin 13 is connected to NET0024; U11 pin 45 is labeled HW_RESET and connected to NET0024. (EPD_Driver.kicad_sch, page 3; SkylabModule.kicad_sch, page 2)"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "J1.13 (SCL) ↔ SPI_CLK ↔ U5.11"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "Clock transitions during display communication can assert the module's hardware reset, repeatedly resetting or preventing normal operation of the WiFi module.",
      "confidence": 0.97
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The EPD serial clock is wired to the SKW92A HW_RESET pin, rather than to the separate clock signal described in the specification. This can reset the main module whenever the display clock toggles."
}

